//@ run-pass
//@ requires: madaros

// Task 5 Step 6/7: adversarial OCSP verification cases, reusing Step 1's
// openssl OCSP responder setup against the same /tmp/chain_test_fixtures CA
// (root/inter/leaf, generated 2026-08-24/25). Each response DER byte array
// below is real openssl output, cross-checked with `openssl asn1parse`
// before use (see ocsp_verify_good.sio's header for the base setup this
// file's fixtures were captured alongside).
//
// Split into one function per case (rather than one large `main`)
// because a single function holding all five ~800-1300-byte DER arrays
// plus their load loops exceeded Madaros's per-function IR instruction
// budget (IR_MAX_INSTRS=16384; measured need was 20654) -- a genuine
// compiler resource limit, not a logic bug, worked around the same way
// this plan's other large-fixture tests stay under budget: keep each
// function's own literal-array footprint to roughly one certificate pair
// plus one OCSP response.
//
// Case (a) revoked: leaf's demoCA/index.txt entry flipped to 'R' via
//   printf 'R\t270825015039Z\t260825042600Z\t2DB4B72D451671EB18CF2720D1938036745C895C\tunknown\t/CN=chain-test.example\n' > demoCA/index.txt
//   (responder restarted -- openssl's OCSP responder does not hot-reload
//   the index file), then re-requested exactly as in Step 1.
//   -> "Cert Status: revoked", "Revocation Time: Aug 25 04:26:00 2026 GMT".
//   Expected: (OCSP_STATUS_REVOKED, OCSP_OK) -- a revoked response is NOT a
//   parse/signature error; err is OCSP_OK, status is what tells the caller
//   to reject it (chain.sio's Task 6 wiring turns this into a CHAIN_ERR_*).
//
// Case (b) bad signature: the good response's own bytes (from
//   ocsp_verify_good.sio) with one byte inside the signature BIT STRING's
//   content flipped at runtime via rawbuf_set (absolute offset 230,
//   confirmed via `openssl asn1parse -inform DER -in ocsp_resp.der -strparse 26 -i`
//   to fall inside the 257-byte signature BIT STRING whose content starts
//   at absolute offset 210 in the full file -- 230 is 20 bytes into the
//   signature value).
//   Expected: (_, OCSP_ERR_BAD_SIGNATURE).
//
// Case (c) certID mismatch: a second leaf ("chain-test2.example", serial
//   2DB4B72D...895D, one hex digit past the original's ...895C) issued by
//   the SAME intermediate, OCSP-queried the same way -> its response's
//   certID.serialNumber does not match `target` (the ORIGINAL leaf,
//   ...895C) passed to ocsp_verify_response.
//   Expected: (_, OCSP_ERR_CERT_ID_MISMATCH).
//
// Case (d) stale: responder restarted with `-ndays 1` so nextUpdate is set
//   (thisUpdate + 1 day: Aug 25 04:26:14 -> Aug 26 04:26:14 2026 GMT,
//   confirmed present via asn1parse's `cont [0]` EXPLICIT wrapper around a
//   second GENERALIZEDTIME), then `now_unix` set 2 days past thisUpdate
//   (`date -u -d "2026-08-27 04:26:14" +%s` = 1787804774), well past
//   nextUpdate.
//   Expected: (_, OCSP_ERR_STALE).

